# API Configuration — LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
#
# Used by `npm run dev`. Do not put the production URL here: `npm run build`
# reads .env.production instead, which already holds the live value.
#
# Nothing needs commenting or uncommenting — the command you run decides which
# file wins.
#
# A relative path, not http://localhost:8099/... — the browser resolves it
# against the origin serving the page, and vite.config.js proxies it to the
# backend. Two things this buys: no CORS preflight, and the same value works in
# production, where nginx proxies the identical path.

VITE_API_BASE_URL=/compliancePortal/
